            0.142
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Figure it Out"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.16,
            0.157,
            0.768,
            0.228
          ],
          "content": "1. Copy the pictorial representations of the number sequences in Table 2 in your notebook, and draw the next picture for each sequence!"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.772,
            0.158,
            0.858,
            0.215
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_4_image_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.159,
            0.236,
            0.768,
            0.308
          ],
          "content": "2. Why are 1, 3, 6, 10, 15, … called **triangular numbers**? Why are 1, 4, 9, 16, 25, … called **square numbers** or **squares**? Why are 1, 8, 27, 64, 125, … called **cubes**?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.16,
            0.315,
            0.834,
            0.411
          ],
          "content": "3. You will have noticed that 36 is both a triangular number and a square number! That is, 36 dots can be arranged perfectly both in a triangle and in a square. Make pictures in your notebook illustrating this!"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.195,
            0.418,
            0.833,
            0.491
          ],
          "content": "This shows that the same number can be represented differently, and play different roles, depending on the context. Try representing some other numbers pictorially in different ways!"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.497,
            0.764,
            0.518
          ],
          "content": "4. What would you call the following sequence of numbers?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.2,
            0.572,
            0.377,
            0.645
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
